      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #44832.\n\nIn `pr-test-{npu,xpu,xeon,musa,rust}.yml`, every `push` to `main` lands in the same concurrency group (`...-refs/heads/main`) with `cancel-in-progress` enabled. Each merge therefore cancels the previous merge's in-flight post-merge run. Recent data: NPU had 39 of its last 60 `main` push runs cancelled, Xeon 18 of 30, XPU 11 of 31. As a result, breaking commits can reach `main` without a completed run on these backends, and the culprit range grows when something finally fails.\n\n## Modifications\n\nIn these five workflows, change only `cancel-in-progress`. The concurrency groups are unchanged.\n\n```yaml\ncancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\n```\n\n- **`pull_request`:** unchanged. A new push to a PR still cancels that PR's older run.\n- **`push`, `schedule` and `workflow_dispatch` on `main`:** runs queue instead of cancelling the run in progress. GitHub keeps at most one pending run per group, and a newer pending run replaces an older one. Runner cost is therefore bounded at one running plus one queued run per workflow, not one run per commit.\n- **`workflow_call` callers** (`release-branch-cut.yml`, `bot-bump-sglang-version.yml`): still never cancelled. The old `!= 'workflow_call'` check could never match, because a reusable workflow sees the caller's `event_name`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A, CI configuration only.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Ran `actionlint` on the changed files. The only findings are pre-existing ones (custom runner labels, shellcheck notes); none are on the changed lines.\n- [ ] Add unit tests: N/A\n- [ ] Update documentation: N/A\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38993339629](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38993339629)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38993339600](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38993339600)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
